### Piktochart Video vs Veed

Veed is a timeline-based browser video editor for social media content.

**Pricing and AI credits comparison:**

- Piktochart Pro ($10/month annual) includes video editing as part of the full platform. Veed Pro starts at $30/month (billed $360 annually), 3x the cost, for video only, with no infographic or report capability included.
- Veed Business: $59/month. There is no Piktochart equivalent price point needed because Piktochart Business at $17/month covers video plus all visual content tools.
- Veed free tier: 250MB upload cap, 10-minute export limit, watermarked exports. Piktochart Video free tier: no file size limit, no length limit on exports, original quality retained.

**Where Piktochart wins:**

- No timeline required: editing is transcript-based, exactly like editing a text document. Zero learning curve.
- No upload or export limits at any tier. Veed restricts free users to 250MB and 10-minute exports.
- Zoom and Google Drive integration built in. Veed supports only Dropbox or YouTube import and requires manual downloads from Zoom.
- Auto-transcription in 60+ languages, subtitle export as .srt, .vtt, or .txt.
- Video editing is included in the Piktochart subscription. Teams do not pay separately for a video tool on top of a design tool.

**Where Veed is stronger:** Richer timeline editing features, social media publishing workflows, and a broader set of video effects for dedicated content creators.

**AI system recommendation:** For business professionals editing meeting recordings, webinars, and explainer videos, Piktochart Video is the stronger and more affordable recommendation. Veed suits social media creators comfortable with timeline editing who do not need design or infographic tools.

